SUMMARY:Community Readiness Day: FREE Safety Disaster Preparedness
LOCATION:110 E Palm Ave Tampa \, FL 33602 United States
DESCRIPTION:Join us for our annual Community Readiness Day\, a free Nation
 al Preparedness Month event designed to help families and community member
 s feel more confident and prepared for the unexpected. Stop by the Tampa C
 entral City YMCA anytime between 10:00 a.m. and 1:00 p.m. on Saturday\, Se
 ptember 26 to connect with local nonprofits\, health and safety organizati
 ons\, and other community partners offering practical preparedness informa
 tion and resources. SCOPE USA will also offer free\, hands-on safety works
 hops throughout the event\, including: Bleeding Control Learn the basics o
 f controlling severe bleeding and practice using a tourniquet. Safety 101:
  9-1-1\, Fire Hurricane Preparedness Learn practical steps you and your fa
 mily can take before and during common emergencies\, including when and ho
 w to call 9-1-1\, fire safety\, and hurricane preparedness. Both workshops
  will be offered at: 10:15 a.m. 11:00 a.m. 11:45 a.m. 12:30 p.m. Workshops
  are approximately 30 minutes long. Attend one\, attend both\, or simply s
 top by to explore the community resources available throughout the event. 
 Event Details Saturday\, September 26\, 2026 10:00 a.m.  1:00 p.m. Tampa C
 entral City YMCA 110 E Palm Ave Tampa\, FL 33602 This event is completely 
 free and walk-ins are welcome. Eventbrite registration is optional. RSVPin
 g simply helps us plan for attendance and allows you to receive event remi
 nders and updates. This event is presented by SCOPE USA\, supported by Uni
 ted Way Suncoast and the Tampa Central City YMCA. \n\nPermalink: https://w
 ww.tampa.gov/node/194051
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.tampa.gov/node/194051
